That settles it, and Sarah's withdrawal of that sentence is the right correction — the office holds no expectation about lectures, so we stop quoting them on it.

For the record, and because a wrong premise was in play: the session times and the seven sections are the office's; who staffs them is mine. My decision stands:

- one TA present at each of my three lectures (Mon 14:30-15:20, Tue 09:00-10:30, Fri 13:20-14:30), as support;
- one TA leading each of the seven quiz sections;
- grading and quiz-section prep split across the three of you.

Bring your proposed split and any real conflict to Wednesday; official sessions come first, and your own blocks get moved around them. That is the last word on it until the meeting.
